-- Slot 4 of the 30-day social calendar: a new recurring content type,
-- mixed alongside the existing 3 daily posts rather than replacing any
-- of them (see 20260823110000 for the schema change this depends on).
--
-- Two kinds of post, alternating through the month:
--   theme 'Trivia'    A real fact about a real glo-temp.com city, sourced
--                     from city-trivia-data.js -- verbatim facts already
--                     vetted for that file (see its own header comment:
--                     "safely-true, widely-documented facts").
--   theme 'Lost city' A real, excavated, dated ancient site from
--                     lost-cities-data.js's `ANCIENT` list -- verified
--                     history, no legend framing needed because none of
--                     it is legend.
--   theme 'Legend'    A myth from lost-cities-data.js's `LEGEND` list.
--                     Every caption states plainly, in its own words,
--                     that the place was never found / isn't real --
--                     the same non-negotiable that file's header comment
--                     enforces for /gem: "A visitor must never be able
--                     to come away thinking Atlantis is a confirmed
--                     location." image_search_term for these points at
--                     a real, documented artwork (Atlantis, El Dorado)
--                     or a real place the legend is set near/named after
--                     (Shangri-La's real Yunnan county, the real Bay of
--                     Douarnenez, the real Land's End coast, the real
--                     Hawikuh pueblo site, the real Lake Svetloyar) --
--                     never fantasy art of the mythical place itself,
--                     which could read as a depiction of somewhere real.
--                     Hyperborea has no such real anchor, so it carries
--                     no image_search_term at all -- social-next-post
--                     already handles that case, serving a plain brand
--                     card rather than nothing (see its own comment).
on conflict (day_number, slot_number) do nothing;
